  "sign_test_cells_with_mean_rank_above_half": "14/23",
  "sign_test_one_sided_p": 0.2024,
  "mean_of_per_cell_mean_normalised_rank": 0.5104,
  "stouffer_z_placebo_vs_real_trade_count": 2.459,
  "pooled_ks_descriptive_only": {
   "d": 0.0962,
   "p": 0.0137,
   "n": 265
  },
  "verdict": "MATCHED. Per-cell mean normalised placebo rank averages 0.51 against 0.500 under the null, and the sign test over 23 cells gives 14 above the midpoint (p=0.202). Placebos do NOT systematically rank low, so the matching is not leaking and the placebo ranks below are interpretable.",
  "history": "Two earlier versions of the base sampler DID leak and were caught by this check. v1 stratified by group and trade-count quantile with round-robin allocation, which at ~1 base per group handed the control arm each group's LEAST active strategy: median placebo trade count 23-30 against 43-68 for the real rows, mean normalised rank 0.57, sign test 16/23 (p=0.047). v2 drew bases before clone collapse, overcorrecting to a base median of 96 trades against a population median of 56. v3 stratifies directly on the ranked population's trade-count quartiles. This is the entire argument for running the check.",
  "pool_choice": "Random entries are drawn from the base strategy's own eligible bars rather than uniformly over the window. Measured cost of the alternative, per the self-test: floor survival 0.883 vs 0.750 and realised/base trade ratio 1.00 vs 0.92 on MGC 60m. Uniform drawing handicaps the control, which flatters every real row above it."
 },
 "anti_overfitting_checks": {
  "look_ahead_bias": "CHECKED, clean. Entry index equals signal index + 1 on 42,279 audited trades (entry_not_next_bar = 0). Signals come from SymbolFrame.snapshot(i), whose cross-timeframe alignment indexes the last COMPLETED bar on each higher timeframe.",
  "one_sided_fill_bias_D35": "CHECKED, clean. The entry price is the fill bar's OPEN plus adverse slippage, never a bar extreme (max observed slippage 2.0 ticks, exactly the model ceiling; entry_slippage_favourable = 0). 321 of 2,602 trades in the probe cell hit a target on their own entry bar - legitimate, because the entry is the open - and in 0 of those was the stop also touched, so no trade was credited a target on a bar the stop would have taken. target_won_a_bar_the_stop_also_touched = 0 across every cell.",
  "understated_costs_and_slippage": "CHECKED and quantified. Commission + exchange fee charged once per side; median cost 0.003-0.017 R per trade. Costs flip 8 of 183 MCL 60m rows and 3 of 37 MCL 240m rows from positive gross to negative net; MGC is barely cost-sensitive (1 of 259). MCL, with a 0.01 tick on a ~$90 contract, is the cost-fragile one of the two.",
  "data_mining_bias_and_deflation": "CHECKED. free_t = sqrt(2 ln n_screened) computed per cell against everything screened, reals and placebos, PRE-collapse: 4.03-4.13. The largest t-statistic anywhere in 28 cells is 2.97 (MCL 60m 180d). NOTHING clears deflation, in any cell, on either contract.",
  "insufficient_sample_size": "CHECKED and it dominates. The 20-trade floor is cleared by 0.7-8.5% of the population; MGC 240m produces ZERO qualifying rows in 4 of its 7 cells. Top-10 rows carry 20-116 trades, and in the disjoint thirds the same rows carry 0-50.",
  "survivorship_bias": "CHECKED. Every generated strategy is scored and retained; the floor-free census is reported beside each floored ranking, including zero-trade counts.",
  "repainting_and_future_data_leakage": "CHECKED structurally. Conditions receive only a FeatureSnapshot, which by construction contains no post-bar data. The placebo schedules are keyed on timestamp and built from signals extracted under the same rule.",
  "parameter_sensitivity": "PARTIALLY CHECKED. Exit geometry is enumerated rather than tuned, and the census reports trade counts by stop multiple. A per-row perturbation sweep was not run.",
  "out_of_sample_and_walk_forward": "The three disjoint thirds are the out-of-sample evidence here. No row is proposed as live-eligible, so no walk-forward efficiency is claimed.",
  "statistical_power": "CHECKED, and this is what makes the placebo result mean something. A deliberate look-ahead cheat - the same entries shifted 5 bars BACKWARD - ranks 1st in all four 274-day cells, with median expectancy +0.30 to +0.76R against a real median of -0.05 to +0.07R, and beats its own base in 15 of 16 matched pairs. The ranking can see a signal that is really there; it simply does not see one in the real rule sets."
 },
